# SynapseCLR Methods

This document summarizes the full experimental methods of:

Wilson & Babadi (2023)  
"SynapseCLR: Uncovering features of synapses in primary visual cortex through contrastive representation learning"

Adapted into reproducible steps suitable for implementation.

---

# 1. Data Sources

## 1.1 EM Dataset

- Source: MICrONS Phase-1 dataset (mouse V1, L2/3).
- Animal: Young adult male mouse, postnatal day 36.
- Volume:
  - ~2,250 serial EM sections
  - Section thickness: 40 nm
  - Resolution: 3.58 × 3.58 nm² / pixel
  - Volume size: 240 × 140 × 90 µm³ :contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}

## 1.2 Segmentation Layers

Three segmentation layers were used:

1. Cell segmentation
2. Synaptic cleft segmentation
3. Mitochondria segmentation :contentReference[oaicite:1]{index=1}

Additionally:

- Skeleton reconstructions of ~397 neurons with somas in volume were used for distance calculations. :contentReference[oaicite:2]{index=2}

## 1.3 Synapse Dataset Construction

- Starting list: ~3.2 million putative synapses.
- Subset of ~6,761 synapses proofread by experts.
- Target training set: 100,000 synapses sampled uniformly. :contentReference[oaicite:3]{index=3}

Final training dataset used:

- 97,658 synapses total. :contentReference[oaicite:4]{index=4}

Includes:

- ~5,664 annotated synapses
- ~91,994 unannotated synapses

