# 2. Input Tensor Construction

## 2.1 Image Channels

Each input example is a **two-channel 3D tensor**:

Channel 1:
- Integer encoding of segmentation labels:
  - presynaptic process
  - postsynaptic process
  - synaptic cleft

Channel 2:
- Raw EM image chunk. :contentReference[oaicite:5]{index=5}

## 2.2 Image Size

Initial chunk:

- 256³ voxels
- Resolution: 7.16 × 7.16 × 40 nm³ per voxel :contentReference[oaicite:6]{index=6}

After preprocessing:

- 96³ voxels
- Resolution: 14.33 nm³ per voxel :contentReference[oaicite:7]{index=7}

## 2.3 Masking Strategy

EM images are masked to include only:

- Presynaptic process
- Postsynaptic process
- Synaptic cleft

Purpose:

- Learn synapse-intrinsic structure without surrounding neuropil noise. :contentReference[oaicite:8]{index=8}

