# 3. SynapseCLR Architecture

## 3.1 Backbone

- 3D-ResNet18 CNN backbone. :contentReference[oaicite:9]{index=9}

Motivation:

- Natural extension of ResNet18 for volumetric data.
- Proven architecture for self-supervised representation learning.

## 3.2 Projection Head

- 2-layer MLP projection head. :contentReference[oaicite:10]{index=10}

Outputs used for contrastive loss.

## 3.3 Representation Dimensions

Explored layers:

- 512-dim backbone last layer
- 512-dim middle layer
- 128-dim projection head output :contentReference[oaicite:11]{index=11}

Primary analyses use 512-dim backbone features.

---

# 4. Contrastive Learning Objective

Framework:

- Adaptation of SimCLR to 3D EM.

Pipeline:

1. Two stochastic augmentations per image.
2. Forward through backbone + projector.
3. Contrastive NT-Xent loss:

   - Minimize distance between augmentations of same synapse.
   - Maximize distance between different synapses. :contentReference[oaicite:12]{index=12}

---

# 5. Data Augmentation

SynapseCLR uses domain-specific augmentations:

## 5.1 Mask Distortions

- Peripheral cutouts
- Shell masking
- Active-zone mask dilation

Encourages learning part-whole relationships.

## 5.2 Intensity Distortions

- Global brightness changes
- Section-wise brightness changes
- Additive pixel noise
- Multiplicative pixel noise
- Gaussian blur :contentReference[oaicite:13]{index=13}

## 5.3 Geometric Transformations

- Translations
- Arbitrary 3D rotations
- X/Y flips
- XY swaps

No scaling or shearing to preserve biological features. :contentReference[oaicite:14]{index=14}

Hyperparameters for augmentations were sampled stochastically within reasonable ranges. :contentReference[oaicite:15]{index=15}

